Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

> do I need a separate response at the household level or can I still use household-level variables to predict the individual-level response Z?

Level-1 and -2 components of observed variables will have the same name at both levels.  Exogenous Level-1 variables are not required (programmatically) to be partitioned into Level-1 and -2 components (see the ?Demo.twolevel help-page example), but they probably should be:

https://doi.org/10.1111/bmsp.12194

> Basically, will this work:
>
> level: 1
> Z ~ X1 + X2 + X3
>
> level: 2
> Z ~ Y1 + Y2 + Y3

Yes, but see above.

Terrence D. Jorgensen
Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics
Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam
http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen

